# Coordinator and Command Patterns

## Coordinator Architecture
The [src/coordinator/mod.rs](mdc:src/coordinator/mod.rs) is the central orchestrator that:
- Manages communication between inverters and MQTT
- Processes commands and routes them to appropriate inverters
- Maintains system health and monitoring

## Command Processing
- Commands are defined in [src/command.rs](mdc:src/command.rs)
- Command implementations are in [src/coordinator/commands/](mdc:src/coordinator/commands/)
- Use the `Command` enum for type-safe command handling
- Implement `to_command()` method on MQTT messages for parsing

## Command Module Structure
- Each command type has its own module in [src/coordinator/commands/](mdc:src/coordinator/commands/)
- Commands should implement proper error handling and validation
- Use async functions for inverter communication
- Return appropriate results that can be converted to MQTT responses

## Channel Management
- Use typed channel data with enums for different message types
- Implement proper error handling for channel operations
- Use health checks to monitor channel status
- Handle shutdown signals gracefully

## Inverter Communication
- Commands should work with the inverter abstraction in [src/lxp/inverter.rs](mdc:src/lxp/inverter.rs)
- Use proper serialization for register operations
- Handle timeouts and connection failures
- Implement retry logic where appropriate

## Modbus Register Operations
**CRITICAL**: All inverter communication must follow the Modbus protocol specifications:
- **Protocol Reference**: [doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md](mdc:doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md) - Complete protocol specification
- **Hold Registers**: [doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md) - For read/write operations (0x03, 0x06, 0x10)
- **Input Registers**: [doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md) - For read-only monitoring (0x04)
- **Quick Reference**: [doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md](mdc:doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md) - Overview and implementation notes

## Register Query Rules
- **Maximum Registers**: 40 registers per query
- **Group Boundaries**: Must start at 0, 40, 80, 120, etc.
- **Cross-Group Queries**: Split into multiple queries if crossing boundaries
- **Example**: To read registers 38-40, use two queries: 38-39 and 40
